    "field": "Carbon-climate feedbacks",
    "problem": "Existing CO\u2082 emission budgets for climate targets rely on a linear approximation of the climate system and largely neglect non-linear feedbacks like permafrost thaw, which makes the allowable emissions dependent on the specific pathway taken to meet the target, not just the cumulative total.",
    "method": "The authors use the compact Earth system model OSCAR v2.2.1, extended with a new permafrost carbon module that emulates four complex land surface models, to investigate how CO2 and CH4 emissions from permafrost thaw impact CO2 emission budgets under different climate pathways.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the reduction in CO2 emission budgets for specific temperature targets that results from including CO2 and CH4 emissions from thawing permafrost, and to demonstrate that this reduction is dependent on the emissions pathway followed to reach the target.",
