            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "S-shaped function for thawed fraction",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "Third, we introduced the theoretical thawed fraction (p) that can take values from-pmin to 1, with a preindustrial value of 0. This corresponds to the fraction of thawed permafrost carbon for a given regional temperature change, but neglects dynamic considerations. The theoretical thawed fraction (p) is fitted by an S-shaped function:",
